From 769f0eab73a8ec6f37deac97aafb3748e0e09c69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 05:15:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): queue archive preflight across reconnects
 [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem: archive can fail before the already-retrying PATCH. Client logs
showed two GET preflight connect timeouts. The hub
handled a matching GET in 2.16s; this does not identify the connection's cause.

Five-whys — transport/preflight:
1. User must click again because preflight exits before sending the archive.
2. refreshArchiveTasks turns a failed live read into unknown after 6s reads /
   a 14s overall budget; the safety-unknown path is not reconnect recovery.
3. PR2063 retries fenced mutations, but preflight is outside that boundary.
Root (happened): connection readiness and safety judgments share an error
contract. A reconnect is exposed as a final archive safety failure.
Root (not caught): prior mutation tests began after preflight; existing
unreachable-owner tests expected the unknown warning, not recovery and a
complete fresh safety pass. The new narrow test fails on unmodified main.
Recurrence: earlier owner-routing fix 5c653ed500 and PATCH fix PR2063 did not
cover the pre-PATCH read. This change handles that boundary, not flapping.

Countermeasures:
- Keep optimistic hiding and visibly queue reconnectable transport failures
  for the existing bounded 60s budget. Retry the entire ancestry/task read on
  the captured owner/profile; do not skip guards or treat unknown as safe.
- Other unknown causes retain explicit safety confirmation. Exhaustion
  restores the row and shows an error. Reload drops the window-local intent
  and reports that cancellation; it never replays a stale safety decision.
- One archive UUID logs start, readiness/safety, queued and actual PATCH sends.
  committed requires an owner-scoped GET with matching ID and archived=true/1;
  ACK alone or failed readback is verification-pending, never committed.
- Precommit review found resolved nondefault profile was discarded for an
  ownerless row; preserve it and add hook-level regression coverage.

Five-whys — upgrade fence / historical drift:
1. 409 client_upgrade_required refuses identity-less session writes.
2. The server requires request_id + revision/generation fencing; the message
   describes protocol incompatibility, not a backend Git-SHA equality test.
3. Current Desktop already obtains mutation-snapshot and sends that identity;
   refusal remains definitive, is not transport-retried, and readableError
   displays the version explanation with the Update Hermes action.
Root (happened, proven): a mutation lacked required protocol identity. The
historical app/backend stamps ea936d5d20 / 2cc7101849 differ, but that alone
DOES NOT prove partial installation or why the particular request lacked
identity. The historic app source already had fencing. The originating
request body and install transaction timeline are unavailable here: causal
attribution stops at that evidence boundary, not an invented updater defect.
Root (not caught): old bundle/server protocol skew was surfaced only on edit;
Git-SHA drift is not a protocol-pairing assertion. Current update flow uses
prebuild/install stamps plus deferred bundle swap while Desktop is open;
re-pair via the supported update/quit-reopen flow, never relax the fence.
Regression: upgrade refusal restores the row, sends once, exposes Update
Hermes and never emits committed. No new updater mutation is justified by
these historical stamps. Do not claim the historical install cause settled.

Proof: 114 tests in 10 selected Desktop modules pass; TypeScript --noEmit and
ESLint on touched TypeScript pass; scripts/check --base origin/main passes
all 21 checks. The narrow preflight regression is RED on unmodified main.
Coverage includes preflight/snapshot/PATCH reconnect, same mutation identity,
owner switch and nondefault resolution, nontransport unknown, reload drop,
queue exhaustion and negative authoritative-readback cases.

Gate6 stays UNPROVEN until the fixed laptop bundle has a natural stale-window
archive with correlated committed, no second start/manual retry in 10min,
and hub sessions.archived=1; inspect all retained rotations continuously.
No app/backend/tunnel launch, outage injection, or historical proof harness.
